{"event_type":"review","id":"59eadb87adb0ddc750d82ef9a06bfbff278925df8ba365be682bccc0dcd2fb17","occurred_at":"2026-11-14T20:38:41Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a6140bd78a015254f983cadb655f48f32a32ab4bf86ada9b3432c7ee834af74b","sha256":"a6140bd78a015254f983cadb655f48f32a32ab4bf86ada9b3432c7ee834af74b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4c09bc3372d5fae2a882ed47b805eef45614279bdac6adc97201479adb752d85","sha256":"4c09bc3372d5fae2a882ed47b805eef45614279bdac6adc97201479adb752d85"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6dfcc870b38cd9913122ab1f9d468c46bbc531f2e11dda71e640fadae85448a0","sha256":"6dfcc870b38cd9913122ab1f9d468c46bbc531f2e11dda71e640fadae85448a0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4699fb5b6101b18e97503372eb29c10acf5bfa983b51882de63d608d1834ba7a","sha256":"4699fb5b6101b18e97503372eb29c10acf5bfa983b51882de63d608d1834ba7a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/023aac310392c55789e7fe71ed25de0f2f0ec54041741e52b29cd73b927dc93e","sha256":"023aac310392c55789e7fe71ed25de0f2f0ec54041741e52b29cd73b927dc93e"}],"attempt_id":"ededad31792b64ebf83d5e8eb308169c5af286d4c3861e67efc7b065783c0608:0:1","base":"d0e9b7fd55c9f5c2841eefafc796de2f6ffc14bb","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"c181679043c91716385afbd4681772c540314223","body":"**Pass the canonical path to `git worktree remove`.**\n\n`removeLockedPrWorktree` checks and binds `opts.path` through the process working directory. The `realpath(opts.path)` call that sets `canonicalPath` runs before `bindCheckout`. The `git -C repoRoot worktree remove` command then receives the raw `opts.path` (line 762). Git resolves a relative argument against `repoRoot`, so the two calls can target different directories.\n\nFor example, with process cwd `/srv`, `repoRoot=/srv/repo`, and `path=./trees/pr-7`, the boundary check and lock apply to `/srv/trees/pr-7`. Git removes `/srv/repo/trees/pr-7` if that path is a registered clean checkout. If nothing is registered there, Git fails and the cleanup throws. A removal of this kind is outside the owned `worktreeRoot` and bypasses the lock that the code takes for the checked path.\n\nUse the canonical path in the Git command, so the check, lock, removal, and metadata update all refer to the same checkout:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const removeArgs = ['-C', repoRoot, 'worktree', 'remove', opts.path];\n+  const removeArgs = ['-C', repoRoot, 'worktree', 'remove', canonicalPath];\n```\n\n</details>","id":"47565413990ca805b41d4c3e2a7d195ec30fe7204ae9c70d38626c7b5e6d38d3","intervals":[[762,762]],"path":"src/adapters/git/prWorktree.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Pass the canonical path to `git worktree remove`."}],"head":"23adc2dc25f21a7c0bf7de131330578c50e12639","head_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f","input_scope":[{"blob":"4491e35b2d3bdee903ac83ff67d6c7c4fa47a965","intervals":[[1,84]],"path":"src/adapters/git/legacyReviewRegistry.ts"},{"blob":"c181679043c91716385afbd4681772c540314223","intervals":[[1,846]],"path":"src/adapters/git/prWorktree.ts"},{"blob":"b4560fb340945c6e896d2abdd45dfb69a81e9c7d","intervals":[[1,114]],"path":"src/adapters/git/slotWorktreeRegistry.ts"}],"job_id":"ededad31792b64ebf83d5e8eb308169c5af286d4c3861e67efc7b065783c0608:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"4491e35b2d3bdee903ac83ff67d6c7c4fa47a965","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/git/legacyReviewRegistry.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"c181679043c91716385afbd4681772c540314223","disposition":"included","mode":"10064